rrier", "label": "Quadratic Proof-Size Barrier in Lattice SNARKs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/snowball/hop2/ref-280-eprint-2025-1220.pdf", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_snowball_hop2_ref_280_eprint_2025_1220_split_and_fold", "label": "Split-and-Fold Paradigm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/snowball/hop2/ref-280-eprint-2025-1220.pdf", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_snowball_hop2_ref_280_eprint_2025_1220_subtractive_sets", "label": "Subtractive Sets", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/snowball/hop2/ref-280-eprint-2025-1220.pdf", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Subtractive challenge sets have only polynomial size (cardinality 2 in power-of-two cyclotomics), forcing lambda/log-lambda repetition and locking subtractive-set protocols into quadratic proof sizes."}, {"id": "references_snowball_hop2_ref_280_eprint_2025_1220_batch_and_lift_over_ring_towers", "label": "Gradual Batch-and-Lift over Towers of Ring Extensions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "references/snowball/hop2/ref-280-eprint-2025-1220.pdf", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Instead of immediately lifting the unstructured projection claim to Rq (quadratic cost), the claim is batched and lifted gradually through intermediate ring extensions, reducing communication to O(lambda)."}, {"id": "references_snowball_hop2_ref_280_eprint_2025_1220_rps_paper", "label": "Klooss-Lai-Nguyen-Osadnik, RoK Paper SISsors (ASIACRYPT 2024)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "references/snowball/hop2/ref-280-eprint-2025-1220.pdf", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null,